# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored). Read by the dev server only, never sent to the browser.
# Leave it all empty for the scripted demo. To run a real agent, say where its model is:

# Where the model is. Leave empty for Anthropic's API. Anything that speaks the Anthropic
# Messages API works: Ollama http://localhost:11434, LiteLLM http://localhost:4000,
# OpenRouter https://openrouter.ai/api, …
AGENT_URL=
# Its key. Leave empty for a local server.
AGENT_KEY=
# The model's name there (default claude-opus-5-5), e.g. qwen3-coder on Ollama.
AGENT_MODEL=

# Optional
# AGENT_ENGINE=codex      run OpenAI's Codex instead of Claude (npm i -g @openai/codex, codex login);
#                         AGENT_MODEL / AGENT_EFFORT then pick Codex's model and effort
# CODEX_BIN=/path/to/codex
# AGENT_EFFORT=low
# AGENT_REPO=/path/to/a/repo
# AGENT_SHORTHAND=off    shorthand mode is on by default: board ops as one line each instead of
#                         JSON, the board read back in lines, terse chat, and (Claude) only the
#                         built-in tools it uses; off gives the standard mode (README, Shorthand mode)
# Claude on Bedrock, Vertex AI or Foundry: set Claude Code's own variables instead (README, Models).
